IF:all
TEXT

Setting the defaults. The first is also the default of @code{m0}.
The second line defines the special characters for the arguments. This is missing the fifth character.
It is thus not possible to select arguments from other stacks than the first stack.

END
CODE
0_chars_pattern:[]-\@+*?~
0_chars_args:$*@#;1;2;3
0_set_var:1;+-+
0_set_var:2;-+-
END
HEADIF:Quoting;all
TEXT

In the next part a macro with a pattern is used to have quoting internal in the macros operational.
The quoting is thus not a builtin function in @code{m0}. 

END
CODE
0_pattern:0string;[@00-@ff]~;stack_b 1 stack_a begin-1
0_pattern:0string;+-+;stack_b 1 +
0_pattern:0string;-+-;stack_b 1 - dup =0 if stack_a end stop endif
0_define:+-+;$1;;nn00 ;0string
0_set_var:3;+-+;-+-
END
HEADIF:ifelse;all
TEXT

END
CODE
0_pattern:m4if;[\(]~;stack_b argpos =0 ifthen abort
0_pattern:m4if;[@00-@ff]~;stack_c 0 stack_a "" 0
0_pattern:m4if;(;stack_c 1 +
0_pattern:m4if;);stack_c 1 - dup =0 if stack_a end ifcmpset stop endif
0_pattern:m4if;[(,][@00- ]*[!-@ff];stack_a begin-1 ;1
0_pattern:m4if;,;stack_c dup <=1 if stack_a end stack_d argnum 3 mod =0 if stack_a ifcmpset endif endif
0_define:\Bifelse(;$1;;rr11 ;m4if;; stack_a argnum =1 ifthen pop argnum =2 ifthen pop pop
END
